{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01DpdB1mNnG6r4iAA1CLk42q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user, local-first productivity system for J.C. Liechty that has grown into two layered things:\n\n- **A personal task/project manager.** It reads and writes plain markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, etc.) as the single source of truth â€” no database. Tasks move through a lifecycle (active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored) with priority/energy/domain/due/notes fields.\n\n- **A self-contained local web app + CLI over those files.** `anchor_gui.py` is the primary interface: a Python-stdlib HTTP server that renders the full dashboard on every request and writes changes back to markdown via `/api/*` endpoints. `anchor.py` mirrors the same logic as a command-line tool and generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **It runs as a persistent Windows service.** The NSSM service `anchor` keeps `python anchor_gui.py --no-browser` bound to `http://localhost:8777`; you open the browser rather than launching it by hand. A 5 AM scheduled health check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) self-tests file integrity, every endpoint, and the R&D surfaces (all model calls stubbed), writing daily reports.\n\n- **It now embeds an \"R&D control surface\" for trio-driven development** (the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill trio). Through v2/v3/v4 it became a per-project \"cockpit\": each project is a row/window with Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass lanes, each lane showing its most-recent session as a status-lit tile that expands inline into a cached summary plus a real, resizable terminal.\n\n- **The terminal substrate is real ConPTY** (the one declared exception to the stdlib-only rule â€” optional `pywinpty`, lazily imported in `pty_manager.py` only), with per-session git-worktree isolation, durable session/preview registries under `.anchor/`, engine toggle (Claude â†” Gemini, Gemini research-only), per-lane doc-role maps, cost/tokens/time rollups, and type-aware deliverable launching.\n\n- **What it ships:** the declared deliverable is **`anchor_gui.py`** itself â€” the running dashboard application. Everything else (CLI, healthcheck, the R&D modules, vendored xterm/brand assets, frozen plan docs under `planning/rnd-v*/`) supports that one shipped surface.\n\nA few framing notes are **design intent locked in plan docs** (the \"calm single-screen cockpit\" North Star, the v4 \"Project Cockpit\"), and per CLAUDE.md v4 was **built and merged to master on 2026-06-13** (9 waves GREEN, 637 passed) â€” so the cockpit is live code, not just aspiration."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ac6dc1c8-ab72-48cf-966d-af5f406fc65f","uuid":"580532bb-79a8-434d-afce-fff957430df2","request_id":"req_011Cc1JR7R4tDSxZ9pjTYfT2"}
